# v0.23.34 — High — the deployment scripts, and five services in a restart loop

This is the topic-level summary of the detailed audit in [`change.log`](change.log).

## Deployment & install

### [V23-50](change.log#L5) — what `setup.sh` and `update.sh` were actually doing · CONFIRMED → RESOLVED

Five services — coordinator-api, pool-hub, gpu, marketplace, trading — were restart-looping with the same import-time traceback:

### [V23-77](change.log#L1926) — node startup could not tell a corrupt schema from a second start · CONFIRMED → RESOLVED

`init_db` wrapped `chain_metadata.create_all(engine)` in an `except Exception` that re-raised only when the message did **not** contain "already exists". The reported finding is that this swallows real errors. Verifying it turned up three more defects in the same twelve lines, all in the path every node runs on every start, and none of them covered by a test — the two functions involved had no test file at all before this.

### [V23-79](change.log#L2102) — a first install never migrated, and the check could not say so · CONFIRMED → RESOLVED

Filed out of V23-75 as *"nothing runs the migrations… no systemd unit in the repo has an `ExecStartPre` that does"*. **The first half of that was wrong and I wrote it.** `update.sh` step 5 has run `alembic upgrade head` for every service with an `alembic.ini` since 1 July 2026, and does it carefully — per-service env file, service stopped for the duration, blockchain-node deliberately skipped.


